{ The King's Head opening is almost like a reversed Damiano Defense. It's not quite as bad, but it still gives black a significant advantage in the opening. It's played occasionally by beginners. }
1. e4 e5 2. f3 { This is the main move of the King's Head Opening. It really doesn't do anything productive for white. While it guards the pawn on e4, it opens up the diagonal to the kingside and deprives the knight from its best square. } *


